    "orientation_quote": "Hexagrams of the Yi Jing [or I Ching] interpreted in base 10, with the top line = 2^5 (most significant bit) and the bottom line as 2^0 (least significant bit).",
    "sequence_context_quote": "There are at least 5 orderings: The popular book order (known as the Wen-Wan ordering, this sequence), the MaWangDui order (A125638), the Lian-Shan ordering (partial), the Kuei-Tsan ordering (partial) and the most recent binary ordering, known as the Fu-Hsi ordering (probably by Shao Yung, +1000 most certainly influenced by Yang Hsiung's Tai Hsuan Jing +10).",
    "academic_reference": "D. E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, vol. 4A, Section 7.2.1.7, p. 486 (cited by OEIS; book not accessed in this audit)."
